course: dictionary
lesson: 11159
title: Names with a capital letter
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word that begins with a capital letter is often a name: of a person, a place, or a thing made by a company. Winchester is a name, so it is written with a big W, just like London or Paris.
explain: «Change here for Winchester, Ashuelot, Nashua, Keene» is a list of stops on a train line. The clues are «change here» and the other names in the list, which are all places. So Winchester must be a place where the train stops.
explain: The same name can mean different things. Winchester can be an old city in England, a famous rifle, or a family name. Look at the words around it to find out which one is meant: a cathedral, a cowboy, or a person.
fact: A proper noun is the name of a particular person, place or thing, and it starts with a capital letter.
fact: «Winchester» is a historic city in Hampshire, in the south of England, with a great cathedral.
fact: Winchester was once the capital of the Saxon kings.
fact: A «Winchester» is a kind of repeating rifle, made from the 1860s and famous in the Wild West.
fact: Winchester is also a surname, and there are towns called Winchester in the USA and elsewhere.
exercise: «Change here for Winchester, Ashuelot, Nashua, Keene.» What kind of word is Winchester here? | *A place name | An action word | A type of food | A colour
exercise: Why does Winchester have a capital W? | Because it is a type of food | Because it is a long word | *Because it is a name | Because it comes after a full stop
exercise: In a Western, a cowboy carries a Winchester. What is a Winchester in this sentence? | A beach of small pebbles | *A repeating rifle | A city with a cathedral | A school for boys
test: In history lessons, Winchester was whose capital? | Captain Ahab | King Arthur's knights | Queen Victoria | *King Alfred
test: Which sentence uses Winchester to mean a rifle? | *The cowboy fired his Winchester at the target. | Winchester is a historic city in Hampshire. | The train stopped at Winchester for ten minutes.
exam: Which is the correct way to write the name of the city in Hampshire? | Winchestr | WinChester | winchester | *Winchester
